{"kind":"artifact","text":"notes/2026-10-04-scope-and-replay-contract.md at exact 7f1ea903cfc36be9252f5fd67b386ea67b96e2b8 on request/scope-contract-r15, under promise git:sha1…c3bb49a on request git:sha1…ff737ac\n\nScope and replay contract, revision 15 at 7f1ea903cfc36be9252f5fd67b386ea67b96e2b8 on request/scope-contract-r15 (two commits on adopted revision 14, fa6417e6). All four subjects; the lane companion and the admission read inventory are unchanged. It is filed together with the authority note's revision 20 at 4ef1a5e3, which it should be read with; where its text says revision 19 of that note, read revision 20. Decision 1, platform code: a platform definition is data plus a rule table under one name and version. A mark in the data, at one of seven kinds of place (an act's grant, a name of also, the type of a field or slot, a written guard, a written effect, a written send, and outcomes by operation kind), says a rule stands there. The rule runs where a written form of that kind would be derived, replaces no written form, and is a pure function of the fold before the entry, the entry's input and time, what the entry retains, and the scope's own earlier entries; it returns only effect and send members, a reason, an item, or yes or no. The check order of section 4.2 is amended for each place; at a grant mark the rule stands in place of the grant check and a pass records an empty authority. A declared definition can hold no mark: the validator refuses each form without its platform option, which no input reaches. A definition with a mark and no rule is unsupported-definition for the whole scope, in the runtime and the verifier. Platform data bytes change; no platform digest is pinned; the two lane digests do not move. Considered and not taken: one appended rule per entry (it cannot stand between written guards, gives a rule's request no result clause, and fails a required slot before the rule runs); replacing the whole row (the data would be documentation only). Decision 2, from the authority note: the member observation's activeKey, the typed content of the rules observation, two windows, and a key's observation counting as its member's for the order of heads, the last taken in both directions, which is one read stricter than asked and is sent back for confirmation. Decision 3, from the I3 source's questions: the form of within; the observation read's request and answer; a revocation refuses before the freshness guards, in a stated four-step order; the fold holds the highest head per subject. Source rows for I3 are listed as I3-1 to I3-11. Open points R1-57 to R1-62 are new, among them the most one rule may return (a stop's outcome can void up to 62 controls, above the written-effects bound) and that no guard bounds the rules observation's content. Reading limits, stated in the note: single writer, no second reader; the I3 source was read in six files and its later questions as written; rule names are proposals and no validator has read the marks. Design only: nothing was run.","body":{"commit":"7f1ea903cfc36be9252f5fd67b386ea67b96e2b8","path":"notes/2026-10-04-scope-and-replay-contract.md"}}